# Density Compare
# Beryllium (Be) — real density 1.85 g/cm³. equal masses: Beryllium vs water — sides ∝ (1/ρ)^(1/3).
scene "Beryllium Density Compare"

element_cube = cube 16.3mm color: #c2ff00 at (-20mm, 8.1mm, 0)
water_cube = cube 20mm material: water at (18mm, 10mm, 0)
# both cubes weigh the same: about 14.8 g — the water cube is the reference
